def nodal(k):
 p=1-1/(k*k);a=2*s.sqrt(2)*s.pi*k*s.elliptic_e(p)
 Q=T('Let ')+r'A,B,C,D'+T(' be independent real standard-normal random variables, each with density ')+r'(2\pi)^{-1/2}e^{-u^2/2}.'+T('Let ')+r'\mathcal L'+T(' be the total Euclidean curve length of the zero set in the displayed square; counting or omitting the boundary does not affect this length almost surely. Find its expectation. The elliptic integral uses the displayed parameter convention.')+r'\quad F(x,y)=A\cos x+B\sin x+C\cos('+L(k)+r'y)+D\sin('+L(k)+r'y),\quad(x,y)\in[0,2\pi]^2,\quad\mathcal L=\operatorname{Length}\{F=0\},\qquad E(p)=\int_0^{\pi/2}\sqrt{1-p\sin^2\theta}\,\mathrm d\theta.'
